              "type": "text",
              "text": "Billy says to Maddy: ‘When I add 10 to the square of a number, the result is 6.’",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-q5-request",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Maddy replies that this is impossible. Explain why Maddy is correct.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The equation gives $x^2=-4$, which is impossible because the square of a number cannot be negative.",
      "worked": "$\\begin{align*}x^2+10&=6\\\\x^2&=-4\\end{align*}$\nThere is no solution because you cannot square a number and get a negative number. Maddy is correct.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
